<h3 id="%F0%9F%92%A1-Key-Findings-&amp;-HR-Insights:">💡 Key Findings &amp; HR Insights:<a class="anchor-link" href="#%F0%9F%92%A1-Key-Findings-&amp;-HR-Insights:">¶</a></h3><ul>
<li>Income Disparity: Employees who left the company have a significantly lower average monthly income compared to those who stayed.</li>
<li>The Low-Income Trap: The KDE Plot clearly shows a massive spike in attrition among employees earning less than $3,500 to $4,000 per month.</li>
<li>Retention at Higher Salaries: As monthly income increases (above $7,000), the likelihood of an employee leaving drops to almost zero.</li>
<li>HR Recommendation: Conduct a compensation bench-marking analysis to ensure entry-level and mid-level roles are paid competitively against the market to stop talent drain.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
