<h3 id="%F0%9F%92%A1-Key-Findings-&amp;-HR-Insights:">💡 Key Findings &amp; HR Insights:<a class="anchor-link" href="#%F0%9F%92%A1-Key-Findings-&amp;-HR-Insights:">¶</a></h3><ul>
<li><p>Lowest Attrition Tier: Employees with a Very High income (&gt; $15,000) have the lowest attrition rate at only 3.7%, indicating exceptional stability.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Highest Risk Tier: The Low income (&lt; $3,000) group suffers from a massive attrition rate of 28.6%, which is nearly double the company average.</p>
</li>
<li><p>HR Recommendation: Retention efforts and salary bench-marking should immediately target entry-level positions to prevent losing staff within their first few years.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
