<h3 id="%F0%9F%92%A1-Key-Findings-&amp;-HR-Insights:">💡 Key Findings &amp; HR Insights:<a class="anchor-link" href="#%F0%9F%92%A1-Key-Findings-&amp;-HR-Insights:">¶</a></h3><ul>
<li><p>Low Satisfaction Risk: Employees with the lowest job satisfaction (Level 1) have the highest attrition rate, with nearly 23% of them leaving the company.</p>
</li>
<li><p>High Satisfaction Stability: Employees with high job satisfaction (Level 4) show the greatest loyalty, with attrition dropping to around 11%.</p>
</li>
<li><p>HR Recommendation: Conduct regular pulse surveys to capture early signs of dissatisfaction. Managers should step in with career development or role rotations when an employee reports low satisfaction.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
