<h3 id="%F0%9F%92%A1-Key-Findings-&amp;-HR-Insights:">💡 Key Findings &amp; HR Insights:<a class="anchor-link" href="#%F0%9F%92%A1-Key-Findings-&amp;-HR-Insights:">¶</a></h3><ul>
<li><p>The Travel Fatigue: Employees who Travel Frequently have the highest attrition rate by far, reaching around 25%, which is significantly higher than the company baseline.</p>
</li>
<li><p>Stable Segments: Employees who travel rarely (Travel Rarely) or do not travel at all (Non-Travel) show much lower and healthier attrition rates, at around 15% and 8% respectively.</p>
</li>
<li><p>HR Recommendation: Frequent business travel is a major turnover accelerator. HR should look into travel fatigue support, introduce virtual meeting alternatives where possible, or offer travel-premium allowances to compensate employees for continuous disruption to their personal lives.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
